    "done_when": "First confirm at base that a review run whose stored record has an unmarked finding yields no audit finding about it, and record that as the base arm. In a new tests/test_an_unmarked_finding_is_refused_at_write.py, built from a review record written the way the production store writes one, not a hand-invented shape: a record with one unmarked finding yields an audit finding naming that finding's file and line; a record whose findings are all marked blocking or follow-on yields none; a record with no findings yields none; and an implement-role run is untouched by the check. The named negative control removes the check, and the unmarked case then passes clean; execute it and record its log. Read the record through the existing reader in reckon/crew/review.py without editing that file, since another live node is changing it; if the check needs a change there, report it as blocked naming the change. The gate is the new test plus every existing test file under tests/ that calls audit_manifest, run at base and at head; list them in the manifest. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. Every pytest process uses a basetemp private to that process. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/scoring-should-stop-a-promotion/an-unmarked-finding-is-refused-at-write.html records the change. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
